The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
fd = memfd_create("uffd-test", MFD_HUGETLB | MFD_NOEXEC_SEAL);
mem = mmap(NULL, mem_size, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_SHARED, fd, 0);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the return values of `memfd_create` and `mmap` are not checked. If `memfd_create` fails, it will return a negative value, and if `mmap` fails, it will return `MAP_FAILED`. Not checking these return values can lead to undefined behavior or crashes when the program attempts to use invalid file descriptors or memory mappings.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (fd < 0)
    ksft_exit_fail_msg("uffd-test creation failed %d %s\n", errno, strerror(errno));
if (mem != MAP_FAILED) {
```
Reason:
The fix adds checks for the return values of `memfd_create` and `mmap`. If `memfd_create` fails, the program will now exit with an error message, preventing further execution with an invalid file descriptor. Similarly, checking if `mem` is not `MAP_FAILED` ensures that the program only proceeds if the memory mapping was successful, thus preventing potential crashes or undefined behavior.

